{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1372600-running-a-mage-war","id":1372600,"title":"Running a Mage War","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-03T19:00:35-08:00","id":1372600,"title":"Running a Mage War","content":"Hey all. So my chronicle has reached its endgame and it looks like the big conflict is going to be my PC cabal of 1st degree masters Vs a cabal of 3 Scelesti 2nd degree masters. My PC cabal will also have a weaker NPC cabal backing them up. So For our year+ long chronicle my PCs have basically avoided a conflict between Mages so I have little experience with what happens when the gloves are off. For those of you more experienced running the game, do you have any helpful hints about a no holds barred mage war?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":565,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","user":"Therian","date":". 03-04-2020, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T19:56:43-08:00","id":1372606,"title":"","content":"Expect asymmetrical warfare, expect rocket-tag, expect chaos. Alternately, be prepared for indirect confrontation. Avoiding open conflict is basically the main reason Consiliums exist as a structure.<br /> <br /> Without a more concrete understanding of what your group anticipates from the phrase &quot;no-holds-barred mage war,&quot; that's about as definite as I can offer: Awakened magic has &quot;this could get very messy very fast&quot; baked into its systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T05:58:48-08:00","id":1372690,"title":"","content":"Some additional factors to consider <br /> <br /> 1- Logistics can tip the tide of wars. Whoever has access to more magical items, transportation (enhanced vehicles, teleportation networks, etc) and supply lines (tass, Hallows, etc) has a powerful edge. As such, these are one of the first things to undermine (poison, taint, usurp, destroy, etc). For example, bags of holding and portable HQs are major game changers, whereas Time mages can completely alter the rhythm of battle (build a fort in moments, cast ritual spells from a time pocket, etc)<br /> <br /> 2- All warfare is based on deception. Since mages are the best equipped to investigate, a great villain doesn't try to hide things from his enemies with brute force. Rather, he uses indirection to point their attention towards something else.<br /> <br /> 3- Never underestimate the power of the mundane. A bunch of armed thugs with heavy wards (&quot;its our prototype hypertech kevlar&quot;) are extremely dangerous to mages due to sheer numbers and Disbelief. Much more so if there is some authority backing it.<br /> <br /> 4- Remember to consider their greater objectives. For example, if everyone has weapons and no one has a clear advantage, then the price of peace lowers to a bargain. So while winning the war may be the best case scenario for the Scelestus, its not unreasonable to think they may want to engineer other scenarios to push their agenda forward. So ask yourself, what do they want to &quot;acquire&quot; and how can they engineer a situation to &quot;lower its price to a pittance&quot;. A Xanatos Gambit is built from that foundation.<br /> <br /> 5- Boons become extremely valuable, acquiring them at a time of urgency is extremely expensive. So calling alliances and cashing in favors can be huge. A Thrysus that acquired a favor from the City Father or an Acanthus who earned a boon from a Changeling Court can have a profound impact on the battlefield.<br /> <br /> 6- Beware the stakeholders. Who has interests in either side winning or losing? How much of their weight are they willing to throw around? For example, fighting Scelestus and Banishers is one thing the Pentacle and Seers are able to cooperate upon, how can that be leveraged?<br /> <br /> 7- Remember to account for the terrain. A Matter mage with proper preparation can lift a house into the air, only to drop it with all their foes. Pitfalls, use of sleeping gas in a closed space or electrical outlets (a Forces mage can do a lot of damage by Ruling the electricity from it) are small yet potent factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-04-2020, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T14:09:21-07:00","id":1374227,"title":"","content":"Unexpectedly, the new Mage Night Horrors has some pretty decent advice on this subject in the Introduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T20:46:27-07:00","id":1374287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1372600-running-a-mage-war?p=1374227#post1374227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unexpectedly, the new Mage Night Horrors has some pretty decent advice on this subject in the Introduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel them very lacking. They are what we know from all 1E - I still have problems to make challenging fights with mages on mages in 2E conflicts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And optional rule 'I know you Imago, so I can counter your spells better' does not seem to fit with mages conflict that works on simple 'who shoots first'. Once you 'shoot' spell, you win. There is no second take on it needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}